# Every path has a human owner, so the pull request rule's "Require review from Code Owners"
# holds the approval that merges to the human named here and never to the account issuebot
# runs as, which has write and could otherwise approve another account's pull request.
* @jleavers

# A change to these paths is a change to what every agent working in a checkout inherits:
# the instruction files it is handed, the sweep skill and workflow it runs, and the CI that
# runs on every pull request. Review one as a change to the agent's privileges, not as
# documentation -- see "What repo-shipped agent text may say" in AGENTS.md.
/CLAUDE.md     @jleavers
/AGENTS.md     @jleavers
/.claude/      @jleavers
/.github/      @jleavers

# The rest of the text an agent reads before it acts, which was not named here (#78). An
# imperative added to any of these reaches the next unattended session exactly as one added to
# the two files above does: README.md and CONTRIBUTING.md are what a contributing agent is
# pointed at, SECURITY.md is what one reports through, and everything under docs/superpowers/
# is text written to be executed -- which is why a separate check requires each document there
# to say up front that its work is over.
/README.md         @jleavers
/CONTRIBUTING.md   @jleavers
/SECURITY.md       @jleavers
/docs/superpowers/ @jleavers
